ules that kernel code calls, and the live-adapter package\n\n- The split (PLAN-197) moved the code of seven kernel entry points into\n  helper packages: five hooks (canonical edit, pair rail, agent spawn,\n  audit log and Bash safety) and two hook library modules (policy and","numLines":30,"startLine":185,"totalLines":2658}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SDLQDJ2VUaRPaateVWiqAC","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
